{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Eightfold.ContactDistributionRank","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Eightfold.ContactDistributionRank","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Choose.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum"],"declarations":27,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.ContactDistributionRank.quaternionicContact_never_rank_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.ContactDistributionRank.quaternionicContact_never_rank_three","kind":"theorem","line":272,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/ContactDistributionRank.lean#L272-L276","doc":"The quaternionic-contact distribution never has complex rank 3, at any `n` —\nits complex rank is even. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.ContactDistributionRank.dim_seven_two_distributions","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.ContactDistributionRank.dim_seven_two_distributions","kind":"theorem","line":263,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/ContactDistributionRank.lean#L263-L270","doc":"**The second pair of different threes.**  In dimension 7 the *Sasakian*\ndistribution has complex rank `3` — what the eightfold needs — while the\n*quaternionic-contact* distribution has complex rank `2`.  They are distributions\nof different rank on the same manifold, and only one of them answers the\nquestion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.ContactDistributionRank.quaternionicContactComplexRank","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.ContactDistributionRank.quaternionicContactComplexRank","kind":"def","line":260,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/ContactDistributionRank.lean#L260-L261","doc":"…hence complex rank `2n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.ContactDistributionRank.quaternionicContactRealRank","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.ContactDistributionRank.quaternionicContactRealRank","kind":"def","line":256,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/ContactDistributionRank.lean#L256-L258","doc":"The **quaternionic-contact** distribution of a 3-Sasakian manifold — the\ncommon kernel of all three contact forms — has real rank `4n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.ContactDistributionRank.bring_cone_degenerate_case","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.ContactDistributionRank.bring_cone_degenerate_case","kind":"theorem","line":249,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/ContactDistributionRank.lean#L249-L254","doc":"**The corpus's own case is `n = 0`, hence dimension 3, hence complex rank 1.**\nThe gap between what it has and what the eightfold needs is exactly one step in\n`n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.ContactDistributionRank.threeSasakian_complexRank_three_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.ContactDistributionRank.threeSasakian_complexRank_three_iff","kind":"theorem","line":242,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/ContactDistributionRank.lean#L242-L247","doc":"So the **Sasakian** complex rank of a 3-Sasakian manifold is `2n + 1`, and it\nis `3` exactly at `n = 1`, i.e. exactly in dimension 7. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.ContactDistributionRank.threeSasakianDim_eq_contactDim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.ContactDistributionRank.threeSasakianDim_eq_contactDim","kind":"theorem","line":235,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/ContactDistributionRank.lean#L235-L240","doc":"**A 3-Sasakian manifold is contact, with Sasakian parameter `2n + 1`.**\nEach of its three Sasakian structures has a contact form whose distribution has\ncomplex rank `2n + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.ContactDistributionRank.threeSasakianDim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.ContactDistributionRank.threeSasakianDim","kind":"def","line":232,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/ContactDistributionRank.lean#L232-L233","doc":"The dimension of a 3-Sasakian manifold: `4n + 3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.ContactDistributionRank.degree_three_but_rank_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.ContactDistributionRank.degree_three_but_rank_one","kind":"theorem","line":211,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/ContactDistributionRank.lean#L211-L217","doc":"The volume form has degree 3 at `dim M = 3` — which is *why* the route looked\npromising — while the object it is a top form **of** has complex rank 1.  The two\nthrees are different threes, and conflating them is the trap this file exists to\nclose. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.ContactDistributionRank.sphere_three_contact_data","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.ContactDistributionRank.sphere_three_contact_data","kind":"theorem","line":206,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/ContactDistributionRank.lean#L206-L209","doc":"And `S³`'s own contact data, named, for the same reason. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.ContactDistributionRank.eightfold_requires_dim_seven","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.ContactDistributionRank.eightfold_requires_dim_seven","kind":"theorem","line":201,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/ContactDistributionRank.lean#L201-L204","doc":"The dimension the eightfold way requires, named. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.ContactDistributionRank.canonicalDegree_eq_one_iff_complexRank_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.ContactDistributionRank.canonicalDegree_eq_one_iff_complexRank_one","kind":"theorem","line":192,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/ContactDistributionRank.lean#L192-L199","doc":"**The degree-1 collapse — the same shape as `VolumeFormDegree`.**  At `n = 1`\nthe canonical bundle `Λ^n_ℂ ξ` is `Λ¹_ℂ ξ = ξ` itself, exactly as\n`Λ^{N-1}W = Λ¹W = W` iff `N = 2` there.  The low case is degenerate because the\nexterior power collapses onto its argument. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.ContactDistributionRank.m_s_fails_either_reading","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.ContactDistributionRank.m_s_fails_either_reading","kind":"theorem","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/ContactDistributionRank.lean#L183-L190","doc":"**Both readings of `M_S` fail, so the contradiction in the corpus does not\nneed resolving to settle this question.**  Whether `ker Θ` has rank 2 or rank 4,\nthe complex rank is 1 or 2 and never 3. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.ContactDistributionRank.dim_five_gives_complex_rank_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.ContactDistributionRank.dim_five_gives_complex_rank_two","kind":"theorem","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/ContactDistributionRank.lean#L175-L181","doc":"The other reading of the corpus's `M_S` (`ker Θ` of rank 4, hence `dim = 5`)\nfails too — complex rank `2`, not `3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.ContactDistributionRank.dim_three_not_complex_rank_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.ContactDistributionRank.dim_three_not_complex_rank_three","kind":"theorem","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/ContactDistributionRank.lean#L169-L173","doc":"Restated as the exclusion: a 3-dimensional contact manifold does **not**\ngive complex rank 3. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.ContactDistributionRank.dim_three_gives_complex_line","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.ContactDistributionRank.dim_three_gives_complex_line","kind":"theorem","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/ContactDistributionRank.lean#L158-L167","doc":"**No three-dimensional manifold can supply it.**  At `dim M = 3` the\ndistribution is a complex *line*.  This is the statement that closes the `S³`\nroute, and it is a statement about the dimension alone — so it holds for all\nthree of the corpus's distinct `S³`s (`S³_AM`, `S³_Reeb`, `SU(2)`) at once,\nwithout needing that ambiguity resolved. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.ContactDistributionRank.complexRank_three_iff_dim_seven","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.ContactDistributionRank.complexRank_three_iff_dim_seven","kind":"theorem","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/ContactDistributionRank.lean#L150-L156","doc":"**The decision.**  The contact distribution is complex rank `3` — the rank\nthe eightfold way needs for `Λ³_ℂ ξ ≅ 𝟙` — exactly when the manifold is\n**seven**-dimensional. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.ContactDistributionRank.complexRank_of_contactDim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.ContactDistributionRank.complexRank_of_contactDim","kind":"theorem","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/ContactDistributionRank.lean#L143-L148","doc":"…and conversely, so the two are interchangeable data. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.ContactDistributionRank.contactDim_eq_two_mul_complexRank","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.ContactDistributionRank.contactDim_eq_two_mul_complexRank","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/ContactDistributionRank.lean#L139-L141","doc":"**The complex rank determines the dimension.**  `dim M = 2·rank_ℂ ξ + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.ContactDistributionRank.realRank_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.ContactDistributionRank.realRank_succ","kind":"theorem","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/ContactDistributionRank.lean#L135-L137","doc":"The real rank of the distribution is one less than the dimension. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.ContactDistributionRank.volumeFormDegree_odd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.ContactDistributionRank.volumeFormDegree_odd","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/ContactDistributionRank.lean#L130-L133","doc":"The contact volume form's degree is always **odd** — so it can never equal\nthe *even* degree an exterior square would need, at any `n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.ContactDistributionRank.volumeFormDegree_eq_contactDim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.ContactDistributionRank.volumeFormDegree_eq_contactDim","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/ContactDistributionRank.lean#L125-L128","doc":"The volume form is a top form: its degree is the manifold's dimension.\nThis is what makes it a *volume* form rather than merely a closed form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.ContactDistributionRank.volumeFormDegree_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.ContactDistributionRank.volumeFormDegree_eq","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/ContactDistributionRank.lean#L123-L123","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.ContactDistributionRank.volumeFormDegree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.ContactDistributionRank.volumeFormDegree","kind":"def","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/ContactDistributionRank.lean#L120-L121","doc":"The degree of the contact volume form `α ∧ (dα)^n`: the top degree. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.ContactDistributionRank.distributionComplexRank","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.ContactDistributionRank.distributionComplexRank","kind":"def","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/ContactDistributionRank.lean#L116-L118","doc":"The **complex** rank of `ξ` once a compatible `J` is chosen — half the real\nrank.  This is the object whose top exterior power the eightfold way needs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.ContactDistributionRank.distributionRealRank","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.ContactDistributionRank.distributionRealRank","kind":"def","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/ContactDistributionRank.lean#L113-L114","doc":"The **real** rank of the contact distribution `ξ = ker α`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.ContactDistributionRank.contactDim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.ContactDistributionRank.contactDim","kind":"def","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/ContactDistributionRank.lean#L109-L111","doc":"The dimension of a contact manifold with `n`-fold symplectic\ndistribution: `dim M = 2n + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}